{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783178-poisonous-blood","id":783178,"title":"Poisonous blood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-09T18:20:55-08:00","id":783178,"title":"Poisonous blood","content":"I currently have a character who I'm going to be running a solo game for that has a great character concept but one aspect (that she is willing to omit) is that because of her characters habit of testing her poisons she'd brew up (brewer kith wizened) on herself that her blood has become poisonous.<br /> <br /> I feel it'd be an interesting detail to drive home that her character truly and fundementally was changed by her keeper but I am unsure if I should allow it or if I do how should I represent it in game.<br /> <br /> So my question is a) should I allow this detail or would it cause problems and b) if I do allow it how do you feel I should represent it on game?<br /> <br /> My current thought is 1L to extract enough for a single does but it must be processed before it is refined enough for use. But for a truly deadly refined poison it would push her to the brink of death and cost 5L. At best though that is a rough thought and far from the best so that is why I am asking here for you fine people's opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T21:58:34-08:00","id":783245,"title":"","content":"I would represent it with merits, similar to the 4 dot arcadian body merit, only instead of upping an attribute limit it would give her blood a toxicity rating (meaning anything that bites her is in for a stomach ache). Then possibly a second merit that allows her to use her own blood to enhance brew attempts. I would only include self inflicted damage if you give her a spontaneous combat application such as splashing opponents and forcing them to resist the toxin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T02:22:34-08:00","id":783309,"title":"","content":"It depends a bit on what exactly the player hopes to achieve. How poisonous does the player expects the blood to be?<br /> <br /> If it is just something that tastes bad or could hurt something drinking the blood I would not worry about it. Just let the player have it. It is mostly fluff. Combat is going to be rare, let alone situations in which opponents actually bite the PC, drink their blood or eat their flesh. Even if you are planning to use a lot of vampires, I doubt it comes up much. Of course, the player could use the blood to mix through drinks and food, but you can easily explain that as the fluff of how the brewmaster's blessing works.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want to let it work like the blood of darkspawn from Dragon Age or the Aliens from Aliens it becomes another matter. In that case though a merit is the way to go. Luckily it is just one player, so balancing it xp wise is not particularly important. Note though that I find the brewer kith's power rather weak, and I would be inclined to accept increasing its power. The venombite kith might be good inspiration to modify it. I also have been contemplating an alchemy/brewing contract that works a bit like the Bloodmagic powers of the Vampires. It is just that I am not sure how to balance it even though something brewing potions that increase a person's size, put them sleep for some time or change them into a toad fit perfectly within fairy tales <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T02:56:46-08:00","id":783327,"title":"","content":"I could definitely just be over thinking it. If they want it to be just a cosmetic detail without any details I'll just let them have it. If they want it to be represented by mechanics I may use the venom bite kith as inspiration.... I honestly had not realized how close that came to what I was looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}